<http://data.silknow.org/object/e74f8cfe-7301-3f24-9f22-98f401a561fa>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Ground:  light neutral linen, very ragged with right hand upper corner gone.  Design:  a wreath enclosing a monogram surmounted by a crown and the date 1704 and a sprinkling of flowers and birds, below this a landscape with a fountain, a shepherd and a shepherdess, and at the bottom three rows of small rectangles filled with conventional all-over patterns worked, in colored silks (several shades of green, blue, pink and violet) and tarnished metal thread."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e822923c-2893-31ca-805f-24d7164aba68> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Ground:  light neutral linen, very ragged with right hand upper corner gone.  Design:  a wreath enclosing a monogram surmounted by a crown and the date 1704 and a sprinkling of flowers and birds, below this a landscape with a fountain, a shepherd and a shepherdess, and at the bottom three rows of small rectangles filled with conventional all-over patterns worked, in colored silks (several shades of green, blue, pink and violet) and tarnished metal thread."@en ;
